<%- include("/partials/head", {
  nav: [
    { id: "settings", label: "Settings" },
    { id: "demo", label: "Grid" },
    { id: "code", label: "Code" },
    { id: "browser-support", label: "Browser support" },
  ],
  title: "Grid Playground",
  description: "A responsive grid with a maximum number of columns and a minimum column width, no media queries.",
  appClass: "grid-playground",
  tour: true,
  styles: [
    "/shared/controls.css",
    "/shared/compat.css",
    "/shared/tour.css",
    "/shared/info.css",
    "/shared/grid.css",
    "/pages/grid/style.css",
  ],
  scripts: [
    "/shared/compat.js",
    "/shared/tour.js",
    "/shared/info.js",
    "/shared/frame.js",
    "/pages/grid/script.js",
  ],
}) %>
      <p class="app__intro">
        A grid that shows <strong>up to</strong> a number of columns, and drops columns on its own when they would get
        narrower than a <strong>min width</strong>. There are no breakpoints: it reacts to the space it's in, so the same
        grid works in a full page, a sidebar or a modal. Each cell is also a <strong>container</strong>, so its content
        can adapt to the cell's width. Drag the corner of the grid or move the sliders.
      </p>

      <div class="controls" id="settings">
        <%- include("/components/control/control", {
          id: "cols",
          label: "Max columns",
          min: 1,
          max: 6,
          step: 1,
          value: 4
        }) %>

        <%- include("/components/control/control", {
          id: "min",
          label: "Min width",
          min: 80,
          max: 480,
          step: 10,
          value: 260,
          unit: "px"
        }) %>

        <%- include("/components/control/control", {
          id: "gap",
          label: "Gap",
          min: 0,
          max: 48,
          step: 2,
          value: 16,
          unit: "px"
        }) %>

        <%- include("/components/control/control", {
          id: "items",
          label: "Items",
          min: 1,
          max: 24,
          step: 1,
          value: 8
        }) %>

        <%- include("/components/control/control", {
          id: "width",
          label: "Container",
          min: 240,
          max: 1100,
          step: 1,
          value: 1100,
          unit: "px",
          sliderLabel: "Container width",
          numberMax: null
        }) %>

        <div class="control control--switch">
          <label class="switch">
            <input class="switch__input" type="checkbox" id="containers" checked>
            <span class="switch__label">Cells are containers</span>
          </label>
          <p class="control__hint">Off = <code>cellNormal</code>: content can't react to the cell's width.</p>
        </div>
      </div>

      <p class="warning" id="warning" role="status" hidden></p>

      <section class="stage" aria-label="Grid demo" id="demo">
        <div class="stage__bar">
          <span class="stage__summary" id="summary"></span>
          <span class="stage__hint">Drag the corner ↘ to resize</span>
        </div>
        <div class="frame" id="frame">
          <div class="demo-grid" id="grid"></div>
        </div>
      </section>

      <p class="grid-note">
        Want the parts of cards in a row to line up (titles, text, prices)? See the
        <a href="../subgrid/index.html">Subgrid playground</a>. Subgrid cards need <code>&lt;Cell cellNormal&gt;</code>,
        because a container can't also be a subgrid.
      </p>

      <div class="compare" id="code">
        <div class="card">
          <div class="card__head">
            <span class="card__title">CSS</span>
            <button class="card__button" type="button" data-copy="css-code">Copy</button>
          </div>
          <pre class="card__code"><code id="css-code"></code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card__head">
            React
            <button class="card__button" type="button" data-copy="react-code">Copy</button>
          </div>
          <pre class="card__code"><code id="react-code"></code></pre>
        </div>

        <div class="card">
          <div class="card__head">How many columns?</div>
          <dl class="stats stats--stacked" id="values"></dl>
        </div>
      </div>

<%- include("/partials/footer", {
  features: [
    {
      feature: "grid",
      label: "CSS Grid (auto-fill, minmax)",
      test: "display: grid",
      caniuse: "css-grid",
      mdn: "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Properties/grid-template-columns"
    },
    {
      feature: "min-max-clamp",
      label: "max() and calc()",
      test: "width: max(1px, 2px)",
      caniuse: "css math functions",
      mdn: "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Reference/Values/max"
    },
    {
      feature: "container-queries",
      test: "container-type: inline-size",
      caniuse: "container queries",
      mdn: "https://developer.mozilla.org/en-US/docs/Web/CSS/Guides/Containment/Container_queries"
    },
  ],
}) %>
